 AND RELAY MODULE, RFRM"},{"id":"ct_mta","partNumber":"(MTA 0301491 terminals - per the MTA drawing)","manufacturer":"MTA","type":"Crimp","gender":"Socket","description":"TERMINAL, FUSE AND RELAY MODULE, MTA"},{"id":"ct_ring_m5_6","partNumber":"GENERIC RING M5 6AWG","manufacturer":"generic","type":"Other","gender":"Socket","minGauge":{"value":6,"unit":"AWG"},"maxGauge":{"value":6,"unit":"AWG"},"contactColor":"Silver","description":"TERMINAL, LUG, RING, COPPER, TINNED, 6 AWG, M5 STUD, ADHESIVE HEATSHRINK"},{"partNumber":"280756-4","manufacturer":"TE Connectivity","type":"Crimp","gender":"Socket","minGauge":{"value":12,"unit":"AWG"},"maxGauge":{"value":10,"unit":"AWG"},"contactColor":"Silver","description":"CONTACT, RECEPTACLE, FASTIN-FASTON 375 (9.5 MM), UNINSULATED, TIN, 3.3-5.3 MM2 (12-10 AWG)","id":"ct_f7_load"},{"partNumber":"160927-4","manufacturer":"TE Connectivity","type":"Crimp","gender":"Socket","minGauge":{"value":18,"unit":"AWG"},"maxGauge":{"value":14,"unit":"AWG"},"contactColor":"Silver","description":"CONTACT, RECEPTACLE, 6.3 X 0.8, TIN, 1.0-2.5 MM2 (18-14 AWG)","id":"ct_relay_63"},{"partNumber":"282110-1","manufacturer":"TE Connectivity","type":"Crimp","gender":"Socket","minGauge":{"value":18,"unit":"AWG"},"maxGauge":{"value":16,"unit":"AWG"},"contactColor":"Silver","description":"CONTACT, SOCKET, CRIMP, SUPERSEAL 1.5, TIN, 0.75-1.5 MM2 (18-16 AWG), SEAL 281934-2","id":"ct_ss15"},{"partNumber":"(ring lug, 8 AWG, M6)","manufacturer":"generic","type":"Other","gender":"Socket","minGauge":{"value":10,"unit":"AWG"},"maxGauge":{"value":8,"unit":"AWG"},"contactColor":"Silver","description":"TERMINAL, LUG, RING, COPPER, TINNED, 8 AWG, M6 STUD, ADHESIVE HEATSHRINK","id":"ct_ring_m6_8"}],"terminalParts":[{"type":"Ring","size":"M8","partNumber":"GENERIC LUG M8 4AWG","manufacturer":"generic","minGauge":{"value":6,"unit":"AWG"},"maxGauge":{"value":4,"unit":"AWG"},"description":"TERMINAL, LUG, RING, COPPER, TINNED, 4 AWG, M8 STUD, ADHESIVE HEATSHRINK","id":"tp_lug_m8_4"},{"type":"Ring","size":"M6","partNumber":"GENERIC RING M6 12-10","manufacturer":"generic","minGauge":{"value":12,"unit":"AWG"},"maxGauge":{"value":10,"unit":"AWG"},"description":"TERMINAL, RING, INSULATED, NYLON, M6 STUD, 12-10 AWG","id":"tp_ring_m6_12_10"},{"type":"Ring","size":"M8","partNumber":"GENERIC LUG M8 8AWG","manufacturer":"generic","minGauge":{"value":10,"unit":"AWG"},"maxGauge":{"value":8,"unit":"AWG"},"description":"TERMINAL, LUG, RING, COPPER, TINNED, 8 AWG, M8 STUD, ADHESIVE HEATSHRINK","id":"tp_lug_m8_8"}],"schematicNotes":[{"id":"n_cabinpower","schematicPosition":{"x":0,"y":-300},"text":"CABIN POWER HARNESS - non-ECU: the glove-box fuse box (Option B, _research FUSEBOX-B-SLOT-MAP 2026-10-11): Bussmann LMI (LMI5-M-2-CB1AD + 3x LMI1-M-1-0, ids hcfb l1-l7), Eaton RFRM 15401-1-2-1-0A (rfrm) and 3x MTA 0301491 (mta1-mta3); the battery feed ring (PDB bus) and the fuel pump run to the trunk. The box lives only in this file. The ECU-switched relays are seated in the box and drawn here (k_fan / k_efi / k_fp on MTA-1, k_str / k_etb on MTA-2, k_fan2 on MTA-3, k_acc in the RFRM, k_eps HCR150 beside the box); their wires land on the module's own relay-position terminals. Fuse -> relay 30 and relay coil+ links are short jumpers inside the box (the MTA 0301491 internal bus is unconfirmed, OPEN-ITEMS row 48). The ECU coil (85) wires stay on ST185-A-cabin / ST185-B-cabin (their ECU pin sets the loom) and arrive broken off. Every feed between this file and A-cabin, B-cabin, CSB3 or EngineRoom-C is drawn broken off in both with a note naming the other file. RFRM / MTA slot numbers are not assigned: cavities are named by circuit."},{"id":"n_cavity_notes","schematicPosition":{"x":4200,"y":0},"text":"CAVITY NOTES - full text of the signals marked * on this drawing\nRFRM EFI86: 5A - relay coil feed, PERMANENT (EFI main relay 86)\nMTA-2 MRS: 7.5A - MRS EPS pump logic enable (fed from k_eps_en 87 per the slot map; k_eps_en not yet in the SoT, OPEN-ITEMS row 40)\nLMI L7: 60A AMI - EPS pump relay 30 (k_eps HCR150, beside the box), Bussmann AMI-60 (60 A, sized 2026-09-28 - sot/channels.csv k_eps c1)\nEFI Main Relay 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Aux 6 / A28 - low-side (Aux 5-8 capable of either; low-side chosen for ECU Hold Power)\nEFI Main Relay 86: Coil + - PERMANENT battery via RFRM EFI86 5A (must stay live after key-off for Hold Power)\nETB Power Relay 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Aux 2 / A20 - LOW-SIDE ONLY (Aux 1-4)\nETB Power Relay 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nFuel Pump Relay 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Aux 3 / A19 - LOW-SIDE ONLY (Aux 1-4)\nFuel Pump Relay 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nRadiator Fan Relay (on/off) 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nStart Relay 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nCondenser Fan Relay (on/off) 85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - -> Ign 5 / B13 - low-side, no external flywheel diode or suppression (on/off relay; INFERENCE from the G4X help Auxiliary Output Wiring PWM-only diode advice, not a Link statement) - TE 1-1393304-0, plain relay, no diode (slot map row 9)\nCondenser Fan Relay (on/off) 86: Coil + - ignition-switched 12V (EFI main relay 87)\nMR-S EHPS pump relay (HCR150,  85: ACTIVE-LOW Coil - <- ECU-B B12 (Ign 6) - EPS relay trigger; moved into the cabin 2026-09-28 (Daniel: every relay in the cabin)\nMR-S EHPS pump relay (HCR150,  30: LMI L7 - Bussmann AMI-60 (60 A, sized 2026-09-28 - sot/channels.csv k_eps c1)"}],"splices":[{"id":"sp_cp_sw12","layoutPosition":{"x":1740,"y":420},"schematicPosition":{"x":1500,"y":3720},"partId":"spp_solder_generic","locationId":"b_bp_1050"}],"spliceParts":[{"id":"spp_solder_generic","partNumber":"GENERIC SOLDER SPLICE","manufacturer":"generic","description":"SPLICE, SOLDERED, ADHESIVE HEATSHRINK OVER"}],"mountParts":[{"partNumber":"1393310-4","manufacturer":"TE Connectivity","description":"SOCKET, RELAY, MAXI ISO (VCF7-1000), 4 POS","id":"mt_vcf7"},{"partNumber":"1-1904045-6","manufacturer":"TE Connectivity","description":"SOCKET, RELAY, MICRO ISO, 5 POS, WITH MOUNTING FLAP (V23333-Z0001-B046)","id":"mt_relay_skt"}]}